Fill the protocol gaps of Jesvi's RedwoodMetal on iOS 16.7 (P13 class check, 2026-11-28).

research\p13-corpus\class-check-167.txt found required methods (queue/encoder/SPI protocols
from MetalTools, counting adopted protocols) that neither Apple's base classes nor Jesvi's
classes implement. Sent to the driver, each would raise "unrecognized selector" in the app
(the blit encoder's forwarding only catches public selectors whose protocol the runtime can
find; SPI ones never). Now answered by name:
- blit encoder (15): optimizeContentsFor{GPU,CPU}Access:slice:level:, synchronizeTexture:
  slice:level: (no-ops: shared coherent memory); resetCommandsInBuffer:withRange:,
  copyIndirectCommandBuffer:..., optimizeIndirectCommandBuffer:withRange: (no indirect command
  buffers: ignored, said once); sampleCountersInBuffer:..., resolveCounters:...,
  {get,reset}TextureAccessCounters:... (no counters); fillBuffer:range:pattern4: (one repeated
  byte -> the library's fill; otherwise a processor fill after the earlier GPU work, in order);
  copyFromTexture:...options: (the copy, options ignored); fillTexture: bytes:length: (one
  pixel repeated over the region through rwa texture_write) and the two color: variants (pixel
  made for R8, RG8, RGBA8/BGRA8 (+sRGB), R32F, RGBA16F, RGBA32F; other formats refused by name).
- buffer (2): iosurface, _aneIOSurface -> NULL (GEM memory, never an IOSurface).
- argument encoder (1): layout -> nil.
Only the count is from the class check; behaviour on the phone is untested (phase 3).

